{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NandhaKishorM/laya/pulls/1420","id":5064644949,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUfqq7c8AAAABLeBZVQ","html_url":"https://github.com/NandhaKishorM/laya/pull/1420","diff_url":"https://github.com/NandhaKishorM/laya/pull/1420.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/NandhaKishorM/laya/pull/1420.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NandhaKishorM/laya/issues/1420","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NandhaKishorM/laya/pulls/1420/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NandhaKishorM/laya/pulls/1420/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NandhaKishorM/laya/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NandhaKishorM/laya/issues/1420/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/NandhaKishorM/laya/statuses/cfd4fd9e61433fab892ad6bbc432c9c583b9ca4a","number":1420,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(cpp): ONNX Runtime backend (laya_onnx) and the onnx lane","user":{"login":"keemsisi","id":7439375,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MzkzNzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7439375?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keemsisi","html_url":"https://github.com/keemsisi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keemsisi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keemsisi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keemsisi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keemsisi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keemsisi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keemsisi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keemsisi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keemsisi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keemsisi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<!-- title: feat(cpp): ONNX Runtime backend (laya_onnx) and the onnx lane -->\nStacked on C4 (#NNNN). Adds the optional `laya_onnx` target: an `infer::Session` over ONNX Runtime 1.30.0 for the fused laya.onnx (+ .data). The core `laya` library stays ORT-free (`-DLAYA_ONNX=OFF` is the default).\n\nORT is pinned and sha256-verified by CMake at fetch (`URL_HASH`): linux-x64 `a5ed5a3cac51fbb2e90da632ae43d19212faaa20e76484e62bcb7c23ddb3b3fd`, osx-arm64 `6ebb5062a934537c352937821f9fe9718e7de1a2db1122a93dd363ffd53a7012`, from https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime/releases/download/v1.30.0/. `LAYA_ONNXRUNTIME_ROOT` overrides and is checked against 1.30.0.\n\nDifferences from Go: no inter-op option; a Session or Agent may be held in a static, closed or not (one process-wide function-local static Ort::Env); the first Open sets `ORT_DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1` unless already set, because ORT 1.30's POSIX telemetry uploader thread can abort the process at exit (\"recursive_mutex lock failed\": it locks a mutex the runtime's statics already destroyed; macOS crash reports from ASan and TSan runs) and starts with the first OrtEnv; a host that builds its own OrtEnv first must set the variable too; Close terminates runs in flight (Go has the same through RunOptions Terminate); the onnx job is advisory like Go's, so the 479 floor blocks nothing until both are made blocking together.\n\nHonest limits: full-multilingual refuses at Open (act_logits declared [1,2], a stale export; Python does no graph check). Local goldens are self-consistent only (no .laya-revision); CI regenerates them. ORT is not instrumented under TSan/ASan.\n\nReview round 1: see REPORT-c5.md table (12 findings, each with a test and a dying mutant where a mutant applies).\n\nReal-weights e2e: per checkpoint singles 89 numbers 0 differ, batch (multilingual) 378 numbers 0 differ, differential fuzz 240 generated states 0 label differences, 1 number off by 1e-4. Final counts (macOS arm64, ORT 1.30.0 osx-arm64 tgz, real english + multilingual graphs, LAYA_REQUIRE_GOLDENS=1, head 94cbc5a7):\n\n| lane | registered | run | skipped | failed |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| ON debug | 479 | 479 | 0 | 0 |\n| ON asan-ubsan | 479 | 479 | 0 | 0 |\n| ON tsan | 479 | 479 | 0 | 0 |\n| OFF debug | 423 | 423 | 0 | 0 |\n\n`--min-tests 480` fails on each ON lane (424 on OFF), so the floors bind.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-29T08:17:29Z","updated_at":"2026-10-29T17:07:04Z","closed_at":"2026-10-29T17:07:03Z","merged_at":"2026-10-29T17:07:03Z","merge_commit_sha":"ccdbfdcfe17bd34a3d56bf8f6a9edc25c9547b8c","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"keemsisi:feat/cpp-onnx","ref":"feat/cpp-onnx","repo":{"id":1384352021,"node_id":"R_kgDOUoOJFQ","name":"laya","full_name":"keemsisi/laya","owner":{"login":"keemsisi","id":7439375,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0MzkzNzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7439375?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/keemsisi","html_url":"https://github.com/keemsisi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keemsisi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keemsisi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keemsisi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keemsisi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keemsisi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keemsisi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keemsisi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keemsisi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/keemsisi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":true,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"Non-autoregressive System 1 decision engine. Typed choice, score and yes/no decisions over any text in a single forward pass, in 100+ languages, with a router that picks the right checkpoint per request.",